John, a software engineer is tasked with designing a portal for EduCommerce, an online learning platform that facilitates interactions between students and faculties.The platform allows faculties to host courses. The system must calculate earnings for faculties based on course enrolllments and provide referral points for students based on their fee structure.
type(class):Educommerce Attribute: Sring courseId String courseName int enrolledStudents double courseFee Methods:The getter, and setter methods for all the attributes,are provided as a part of the code skeleton Responsibilies:Include a parameterized constructor of four arguments in the following order-courseId,courseName,enrolledStudents and courseFee Include the abstract method in the EduCommerce class abstract public, double computeEarnings()
type(class):StudentPortal Attribute:double referralPoints Methods:The getter, and setter methods for the attribute,are provided as a part of the code skeleton Responsibilies:Include a public 4 argument constructor of four arguments in the following order-courseId,courseName,enrolledStudents and courseFee.
type(class):StudentPortal Methods:computeEarnings Responsibilies:The method sets the value for referralPOints based on the courseFee Constraints:When the courseFee is more than 5000, set the referralPoints as(int)(couseFee/100)Otherwise,set the referralPoints to 0. If enrolledStudents or courseFee is less than or equal to 0,then set the value for referralPoints as 0 and return -1.0. The referralPoints should be returned as double
type(class):FacultyPortal Attribute:String facultyCategory Methods:Methods:The getter, and setter methods for the attribute,are provided as a part of the code skeleton.  Responsibilies:Include a public 4 argument constructor of four arguments in the following order-courseId,courseName,enrolledStudents and courseFee.
type(class):FacultyPortal Methods:computeEarnings Responsibilities:The method calculates the total earnings and sets the value for the facultyCategory based on the calculated total earnings. Constraints:The total earnings is caluclated as the product of number of students enrolled and courseFee. When the total earnings is greater than or equal to 7000,then set the value for the facultyCategory as "Experienced Faculty".Otherwise set the value for the facultyCategory as "Intermediate Faculty". If enrolledStudents or CouseFee is less than or equal to 0,then set the value for facultyCategory as "No Category",and return -1.0. The calculated total earnings should be returned as double.
note:The platform name can be either "StudentPortal" or "FacultyPortal"(case-insensitive)
the StudentPortal and FacultyPortal class implements abstract methods of the EduCommerce class
Edit only the StudentPortal and FacultyPortal classes to implement the business requirements.
Assume that all the inputs are valid.
The methods and the constructor should be public,and the attribues of the class should be private.
